## 1. Compact wired to the page — full load AND htmx refresh path
`internal/handlers/insights/handlers.go:225-286` (handleInsights) is the
ONLY handler for GET /insights. The page's htmx refresh
(`hx-get="/insights" hx-target="#insights-wrapper" hx-select="#insights-wrapper"`,
web/templates/pages/insights.html:7) re-issues the same GET /insights
request — there is no separate content-only handler — so both the full page
load and the htmx-refresh path execute the identical
`_ = renderer.Render(w, "base", pageData)` call, which includes
`insights.html:41`:
`{{template "shared/period-context" (dict "Period" .Period "Compact" true)}}`.
Corroborating existing test (unmodified, RF3/SV1/LT1/DI2 family):
`TestDI2InsightsPeriodFullAndPartials` (internal/handlers/insights/period_di2_test.go)
calls handleInsights directly with HX-Request header both false and true for
`/insights` and asserts period-context content renders in both — confirms
structurally that both paths funnel through handleInsights.
$ go test ./internal/handlers/insights/... -run 'TestDI2InsightsPeriodFullAndPartials' -v
--- PASS: TestDI2InsightsPeriodFullAndPartials (0.10s)

New page-level test (part of the manifest) directly renders "insights-content"
(the same define handleInsights's "base" template includes) with a Stale and
fresh Period and asserts no card chrome + Compact section wrapper +
conditional "Note:" callout:
$ go test ./internal/templates/... -run TestIP1PageWiresCompactPeriodContext -v
--- PASS: TestIP1PageWiresCompactPeriodContext (0.03s)
    --- PASS: .../stale (0.01s)
    --- PASS: .../fresh (0.01s)

