## 7. Split classification (severity / direction single source)
$ rtk proxy git diff master -- web/templates/components/insights-investigation.html internal/handlers/insights/investigation.go
Severity: `investigation.go` sets `FindingView.Severity` directly from
`a.Severity` (the anomaly service's own field) at the single `add(...)` call
site for anomaly findings; price-creep findings pass `""`. Template only
does `{{if eq .Severity "high"}}`/`"medium"` — no re-derivation.
Direction: insights.html's new Change/contributor tiles use
`.Change.Direction` ("up"/"down") exclusively — the same field
"insights-change-cell"/"insights-dollar-change" already consumed on master;
no new direction logic invented.

## 8. Edge cases (item 7 of original brief)
- HistoryAvailable=false branch: template else-arm renders only the Selected
  tile (single-column grid) + "Not enough history to compare" — confirmed by
  reading web/templates/pages/insights.html:85-90 and by
  TestIP1NeutralTileBorderContrast's tile count (6 = Selected+Prior+Change+3
  strip links, all under the HistoryAvailable=true arm).
- Zero-row group + strip link: `insights-recurring-group`
  (insights-investigation.html:27-29) renders `id="recurring-{{.Group.ID}}"`
  on the <h3> unconditionally — the table/detail body is the only part gated
  on `{{if .Group.Rows}}` — so a strip tile's `#recurring-{{.ID}}` anchor
  always resolves even for a 0-row group.
- Legacy "Other recurring spending" ({{else}} compatibility branch,
  insights.html:199-201) is a different code path (keyed off
  `.Insights.OtherRecurring`, not `.Groups`) untouched by this task; not
  reachable when `.Investigation` is present (the real handler always
  supplies it), consistent with master.

